[size=16pt][b]RUN 28: BITCOIN MACHINE CODE vs BITCOIN CORE v31.1[/b][/size]

[i]A from-genesis mainnet sync, measured from the nodes' own logs, 2026-09-19 to 2026-09-21[/i]

"The Measuring Equipment" (2026-09-19) left two numbers marked PENDING: an unpolled rerun of Core v31.1 and run 28, a fresh bmc sync on the current code with nothing calling its RPC. Both runs have finished. This post gives their results, how they were measured, and what was not clean about them.

[hr]
[size=12pt][b]The result[/b][/size]

[table]
[tr][td][/td][td][b]bmc, run 28[/b][/td][td][b]Core v31.1, rerun[/b][/td][/tr]
[tr][td]start[/td][td]2026-09-20 21:36:53Z[/td][td]2026-09-19 14:28:33Z[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]end of IBD, from its own log[/td][td]2026-09-21 16:00:55Z ([tt][dlc] catch-up done[/tt])[/td][td]2026-09-20 10:01:27Z ([tt]Leaving InitialBlockDownload[/tt])[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]elapsed to the end of IBD[/b][/td][td][b]18 h 24 m 02 s[/b][/td][td][b]19 h 32 m 54 s[/b][/td][/tr]
[tr][td]elapsed to the live tip[/td][td]18 h 25 m 28 s (height 967,924)[/td][td]19 h 33 m 09 s (height 967,813)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]UTXO set[/td][td]MuHash identical to Core at 968,025[/td][td][/td][/tr]
[/table]

[b]bmc finished 1 h 08 m 52 s sooner, 5.9% of Core's time.[/b]

The UTXO set check ran after the sync. The harness turned off bmc's networking, waited for a stable height, and compared bmc's MuHash with a separate Core v31.1 node at the same height:

[quote][tt]2026-09-21T17:45:46Z PASS muhash identical at 968025 (6e867a52c419fef00cec1768da7e8fbdf38a610c410cd4c4d01f02eef017fe2e)[/tt]
[i]-- run28/phase.log[/i][/quote]

[hr]
[size=12pt][b]How it was measured[/b][/size]

Both runs used the same machine and the same drive, one after the other:

[list][li]AMD Ryzen 9 9950X3D (16 cores, 32 threads), 123 GiB RAM[/li][li]Corsair MP600 PRO XT 8 TB NVMe for both datadirs[/li][li]the public mainnet peer-to-peer network, no local peers[/li][/list]

Both nodes had the same settings:

[table]
[tr][td][b]setting[/b][/td][td][b]bmc[/b][/td][td][b]Core[/b][/td][/tr]
[tr][td]dbcache[/td][td]8192[/td][td]8192[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]txindex, blockfilterindex, coinstatsindex[/td][td]on[/td][td]on[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]maxconnections[/td][td]48[/td][td]48[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]peers downloading blocks at once[/td][td]8[/td][td]8 (fixed in Core)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]assumevalid[/td][td]Core's default block, height 938,343[/td][td]default, same block[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]CPU niceness[/td][td]0[/td][td]0 (systemd default)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]build[/td][td]commit [tt]1562ae86[/tt][/td][td]v31.1 release, built from source[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[b]Nobody called either node's RPC during IBD.[/b] This rule was added after run 27, when a monitoring tool polled that run for 14 hours. Its polls made bmc's RPC side read 10.2 TB from disk, and each [tt]gettxoutsetinfo[/tt] sent to the first Core baseline forced a UTXO cache flush. This time, all progress came from each node's own log. The IBD-end times in the tables are timestamps written by the nodes themselves, not the moment a monitor noticed.

[hr]
[size=12pt][b]Time to height[/b][/size]

The heights come from each node's own log: bmc's [tt][utxo_live] catchup progress: height=N[/tt] and Core's [tt]UpdateTip ... height=N[/tt]. Elapsed time is counted from each run's start. The segment columns give the time each node took for that stretch of 100,000 blocks.

[table]
[tr][td][b]height[/b][/td][td][b]bmc elapsed[/b][/td][td][b]Core elapsed[/b][/td][td][b]bmc ahead by[/b][/td][td][b]%[/b][/td][td][b]bmc segment[/b][/td][td][b]Core segment[/b][/td][/tr]
[tr][td]100,000[/td][td]0:02:58[/td][td]0:06:01[/td][td]0:03:03[/td][td]50.7%[/td][td]0:02:58[/td][td]0:06:01[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]200,000[/td][td]0:08:52[/td][td]0:11:25[/td][td]0:02:33[/td][td]22.3%[/td][td]0:05:54[/td][td]0:05:24[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]300,000[/td][td]0:30:49[/td][td]0:36:14[/td][td]0:05:25[/td][td]14.9%[/td][td]0:21:57[/td][td]0:24:49[/td][/tr]
